{"annotations":{"openWorldHint":true,"readOnlyHint":true},"description":"Public-record due-diligence facts for a US residential address. Any US address: FEMA flood zone at the geocoded point, HUD FY2026 Small Area FMR (or area FMR) by bedrooms, and a property-tax estimate: official rates in Nashville (Metro rate), Denver (levy by tax district), Chicago (Cook County tax code) and Maricopa County cities (tax area code), elsewhere a rough county-level estimate from Census ACS, labeled as such. Full parcel-level coverage (zoning district, overlays, STR permit eligibility for owner-occupied vs non-owner-occupied, caps, existing STR permits/licenses) only in Nashville/Davidson County TN, Denver CO, Scottsdale AZ, Chicago IL (building size, Prohibited Buildings List, Restricted Residential Zones), and Boise ID (City of Boise and unincorporated Ada County; zoning district plus Idaho Code 67-6539 state STR rules). New York City (city-wide rules plus a per-building Prohibited Buildings List and registration check by BIN) and Austin TX (city-wide rules plus a per-parcel full/limited-purpose/ETJ check) are also covered, as are Phoenix, Mesa, Tempe, and Tucson (city limits) AZ (city-wide rules); str.granularity says which. Elsewhere zoning/STR return not_covered. Every value carries a source and as-of date. HOA/deed restrictions are not checked. Informational only; not legal/tax/insurance/lending advice. Same tool as nashville_deal_check. Status values. Top-level status: ok = every evaluated section answered; needs_review = partial answer, at least one section needs a person or a retry (read each section's status and the warnings); unavailable = no section could be answered (address not found, or every source failed); out_of_scope = no evaluated section applies at this address. Section status uses the same words plus not_covered (this area is not evaluated). str.status follows the two permit determinations: new_non_owner_occupied_permit.value (allowed, not_allowed, needs_review, out_of_scope, not_covered, unavailable) and owner_occupied_permit.value (possible, not_allowed, needs_review, out_of_scope, not_covered, unavailable). Both firm = ok, one firm and one not = needs_review, none usable = unavailable. str.supporting_data_status appears when side lookups such as permit counts or building lists were incomplete.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"address":{"description":"US street address including city and state, e.g. '321 50th Ave N, Nashville, TN'","type":"string"},"bedrooms":{"description":"For HUD rent benchmark. Defaults to 2.","maximum":4,"minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"include":{"items":{"enum":["rent","tax","flood","str","zoning"]},"type":"array"},"value":{"description":"Optional purchase price or value in USD. Echoed in query.value. Where no Assessor value exists it drives property_tax.estimated_annual_tax; where one exists, the estimate at your value is in property_tax.estimate_at_your_value.","type":"number"}},"required":["address"],"type":"object"},"name":"ziplot_deal_check","outputSchema":{"properties":{"api_version":{"type":"string"},"attribution":{"items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"coverage":{"properties":{"area":{"type":"string"},"full_coverage_areas":{"items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"level":{"enum":["full","basic"],"type":"string"}},"required":["level","area","full_coverage_areas"],"type":"object"},"disclaimer":{"type":"string"},"error":{"description":"Present only when an upstream failed and the caller should retry (isError true).","properties":{"code":{"enum":["upstream_timeout","upstream_error"],"type":"string"},"message":{"type":"string"},"retry_after_seconds":{"type":"integer"},"upstream":{"type":"string"}},"required":["code","upstream","message","retry_after_seconds"],"type":"object"},"flood":{"properties":{"fema_zone":{"anyOf":[{"properties":{"basis":{"const":"geocoded_point"},"dfirm_id":{"type":["string","null"]},"in_sfha":{"type":["boolean","null"]},"source":{"description":"Where the value comes fro